Let my soul rejoice in the Lord, for He hath clothed me with the garment of salvation, and with the robe of gladness hath He covered me; as upon a bridegroom He hath placed a crown upon me,

=== LEAF p165 === (Fol. 83r)
and as a bride hath He adorned me with beauty. And as the earth causes her flower to grow, and as a garden causes its seeds to shoot forth, so shall the Lord cause righteousness to shine forth, and joy before all the nations. For Zion's sake I will not keep silence, and for Jerusalem's sake I will not hold My peace, until My righteousness go forth as light, and My salvation shall burn as a torch. And the nations shall see thy righteousness, and all the earthly kings thy glory; and thou shalt be called by thy new name, which the Lord shall name. And thou shalt be a crown of comeliness in the hand of the Lord, and a royal diadem in the hand of thy God. And thou shalt no more be called Forsaken, neither shall thy land any more be called Desolate; for thy name shall be called My Pleasure, and thy land the Inhabited Earth; for the Lord is well pleased in thee, and thy land shall be inhabited. And as a young man dwells with a virgin, so shall thy Creator dwell with thee;

